WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:59.143
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:59.413 --> 01:03.908
[Apocalypse Log 16]

3
01:16.833 --> 01:18.291
Where did you go?

4
01:18.291 --> 01:19.458
I just went to the canteen.

5
01:19.458 --> 01:21.833
I was afraid the food would run out.

6
01:21.833 --> 01:23.375
It's okay, I'm not hungry.

7
01:23.375 --> 01:25.475
Give it to Grandma Qiu and the others.

8
01:28.041 --> 01:30.030
Granny Qiu.

9
01:31.416 --> 01:33.932
He Yao, what are you doing?

10
01:38.291 --> 01:41.181
Stop fighting! Lie, stop!

11
01:44.041 --> 01:45.625
Are you crazy?

12
01:45.625 --> 01:48.419
Dr. He is treating Granny Qiu's injury.

13
01:50.500 --> 01:52.166
You liar!

14
01:52.166 --> 01:54.000
How dare you show up here?

15
01:54.000 --> 01:55.375
You...

16
01:55.375 --> 01:57.416
Foolish!

17
01:57.416 --> 01:59.500
You two fools!

18
01:59.500 --> 02:01.971
Dr. He is helping me.

19
02:05.666 --> 02:07.583
I was moving things just now and wasn't careful.

20
02:07.583 --> 02:09.166
I dislocated my shoulder.

21
02:09.166 --> 02:10.500
It hurts like hell.

22
02:10.500 --> 02:13.458
Dr. He is resetting it for me.

23
02:13.458 --> 02:17.572
How can you hit someone without even asking what's going on?

24
02:19.583 --> 02:20.791
I'm fine.

25
02:20.791 --> 02:21.833
Calm down, everyone.

26
02:21.833 --> 02:23.592
It's just a misunderstanding.

27
02:25.708 --> 02:26.999
Granny Qiu.

28
02:26.999 --> 02:28.083
Try moving your shoulder.

29
02:28.083 --> 02:30.066
Is it okay now?

30
02:33.541 --> 02:34.916
Yes.

31
02:34.916 --> 02:36.125
It's better.

32
02:36.125 --> 02:37.750
Thank you, Dr. He.

33
02:37.750 --> 02:38.916
It's nothing.

34
02:38.916 --> 02:39.958
I have a bit of a...

35
02:39.958 --> 02:41.625
small misunderstanding with them.

36
02:41.625 --> 02:43.166
You two.

37
02:43.166 --> 02:45.183
Let's talk over there.

38
02:49.083 --> 02:50.375
Don't fight.

39
02:50.375 --> 02:52.083
Talk things out calmly.

40
02:52.083 --> 02:53.622
Don't worry, Grandma.

41
03:05.458 --> 03:07.666
Why did you steal our car?

42
03:07.666 --> 03:09.416
It was an emergency. I had to leave.

43
03:09.416 --> 03:11.532
And I didn't want to involve you.

44
03:17.000 --> 03:18.250
Fine.

45
03:18.250 --> 03:21.120
I admit that what I did was wrong.

46
03:23.333 --> 03:25.333
Lin Zai, I'm sorry.

47
03:25.333 --> 03:26.833
But I really didn't mean to harm you.

48
03:26.833 --> 03:28.791
Then why are you here?

49
03:28.791 --> 03:31.037
Don't tell me it's another coincidence.

50
03:32.083 --> 03:34.041
I couldn't find my brother.

51
03:34.041 --> 03:36.583
I drove here, and bumped into Dao and the others.

52
03:36.583 --> 03:37.750
So, I'm staying at this camp for now.

53
03:37.750 --> 03:39.750
Where's the car?

54
03:39.750 --> 03:40.916
The car is right in the back.

55
03:40.916 --> 03:41.916
I'll take you there.

56
03:41.916 --> 03:43.875
Let's just move on from this, all right?

57
03:43.875 --> 03:46.545
Whether we move on is up to me.

58
03:55.166 --> 03:57.041
When did you get injured?

59
03:57.041 --> 03:59.045
It's nothing, just a minor wound.

60
03:59.750 --> 04:01.625
Don't move. The wound is so deep.

61
04:01.625 --> 04:03.266
Why didn't you say anything?

62
04:07.416 --> 04:10.157
Now, lead the way to the car.

63
04:12.666 --> 04:15.115
What tricks are you trying to pull now?

64
04:17.000 --> 04:18.728
I'll take you there.

65
04:43.500 --> 04:45.219
You can have it back.

66
04:48.458 --> 04:50.125
It's out of fuel.

67
05:06.875 --> 05:08.125
I didn't even notice.

68
05:08.125 --> 05:10.212
There's actually a barrel of fuel here.

69
05:12.958 --> 05:14.750
This must be the camp's reserve fuel.

70
05:14.750 --> 05:16.750
It's an important resource.

71
05:16.750 --> 05:18.496
We shouldn't just use it like this.

72
05:19.417 --> 05:20.583
Lin Zai is right.

73
05:20.583 --> 05:22.375
It belongs to someone else, after all.

74
05:23.250 --> 05:25.600
Do you even have a say in this?

75
05:30.541 --> 05:32.508
Lie, watch your tone.

76
05:33.334 --> 05:34.833
This fuel already has an owner.

77
05:34.833 --> 05:36.716
Besides, we're not in a hurry to leave.

78
05:39.375 --> 05:41.500
Are you not in a hurry to leave,

79
05:41.500 --> 05:43.640
or do you just not want to come with me?

80
05:44.916 --> 05:46.843
What do you mean by that?

81
05:47.583 --> 05:50.798
If you're in such a hurry, then leave by yourself.

82
05:52.250 --> 05:53.713
Lin Zai!

83
06:14.250 --> 06:16.333
Chang Huan, I met someone.

84
06:16.333 --> 06:17.333
He's just like you.

85
06:17.333 --> 06:18.958
His wounds heal at an astonishing rate,

86
06:18.958 --> 06:21.292
but he shows no signs of turning.

87
06:21.292 --> 06:24.333
I suspect it's an abnormal evolution

88
06:24.333 --> 06:26.708
that occurs after resisting the zombie virus.

89
06:26.708 --> 06:28.620
I'll do whatever it takes to keep him here.

90
06:28.620 --> 06:31.208
If he is an immune body,

91
06:31.208 --> 06:34.597
our experiment will surely succeed.

92
06:46.958 --> 06:48.250
The three of you...

93
06:48.250 --> 06:50.937
didn't have further conflict, did you?

94
06:51.708 --> 06:56.254
Dr. He doesn't seem like a bad person to me.

95
06:58.250 --> 06:59.875
The misunderstanding is cleared up.

96
06:59.875 --> 07:01.583
It's fine.

97
07:01.583 --> 07:04.208
Dr. He... is a bit of a loner,

98
07:04.208 --> 07:05.833
but he's a good man.

99
07:05.833 --> 07:08.144
You young people...

100
07:16.458 --> 07:17.500
You're being too rough.

101
07:17.500 --> 07:19.541
Don't hurt Grandma.

102
07:19.541 --> 07:21.583
All right.

103
07:21.583 --> 07:23.375
I feel better after moving around.

104
07:23.375 --> 07:24.625
You two must be tired.

105
07:24.625 --> 07:27.541
Go back and get some rest.

106
07:27.541 --> 07:28.875
It's okay, Grandma.

107
07:28.875 --> 07:29.958
I'll walk you back.

108
07:29.958 --> 07:31.510
Let's go.

109
09:03.708 --> 09:05.916
We're in luck today.

110
09:05.916 --> 09:08.166
Caught a little something.

111
09:08.166 --> 09:10.125
I'll clean them up in a bit.

112
09:10.125 --> 09:13.250
I'll add some fresh flavor for everyone.

113
09:13.250 --> 09:15.068
Take a look.

114
09:17.000 --> 09:20.000
Great! We haven't had meat in ages.

115
09:20.000 --> 09:23.958
Sir, can I have this sand crab?

116
09:23.958 --> 09:25.916
- This one? - Yes.

117
09:25.916 --> 09:27.583
It's so small, there's no meat.

118
09:27.583 --> 09:29.708
What do you want it for?

119
09:29.708 --> 09:31.283
Just let me have it.

120
09:32.333 --> 09:34.083
Give it to him.

121
09:34.083 --> 09:36.012
All right, it's yours.

122
09:41.017 --> 09:43.791
In a while, I'll finish cleaning and make a stew.

123
09:43.791 --> 09:46.125
I'll improve the rations for everyone tonight.

124
09:46.125 --> 09:48.617
- Sound good? - Yeah!

125
09:57.125 --> 09:58.430
Lin Zai.

126
09:59.416 --> 10:00.881
This is for you.

127
10:01.833 --> 10:03.660
I remember you like these.

128
10:04.916 --> 10:06.000
I don't need it.

129
10:06.000 --> 10:07.521
Take it away.

130
10:20.291 --> 10:21.666
It's a gift.

131
10:21.666 --> 10:24.291
The apocalypse has taken a lot from me.

132
10:24.291 --> 10:26.125
So, I want to cherish the people I meet,

133
10:26.125 --> 10:27.833
people I can rely on.

134
10:27.833 --> 10:31.750
I think we could become companions who are like family.

135
10:31.750 --> 10:33.416
Used to being abandoned.

136
10:34.458 --> 10:37.083
Discarding others to save yourself...

137
10:37.083 --> 10:39.083
Isn't that just human instinct?

138
10:39.083 --> 10:40.916
I'm not like them.

139
10:40.916 --> 10:42.625
I have a heart.

140
10:48.291 --> 10:49.992
I will protect you...

141
10:51.458 --> 10:53.073
with my life.

142
11:11.916 --> 11:13.208
Thank you.

143
11:13.208 --> 11:14.621
Go back.

144
11:15.708 --> 11:18.036
So, are you still mad at me?

145
11:20.958 --> 11:23.083
I'm not mad at you.

146
11:23.083 --> 11:25.625
- Then why... - Too much has happened lately.

147
11:25.625 --> 11:27.044
My mind is a bit of a mess.

148
11:27.810 --> 11:30.250
I need to clear my head first.

149
11:30.250 --> 11:31.736
You should go.

150
12:03.750 --> 12:05.102
Come in.

151
12:07.665 --> 12:09.000
I just prepared some herbs.

152
12:09.000 --> 12:10.250
I'm taking them to Grandma Qiu.

153
12:10.250 --> 12:12.066
I thought I'd stop by and see you.

154
12:13.416 --> 12:15.210
You have a pet?

155
12:16.375 --> 12:18.141
I found it on the road.

156
12:21.291 --> 12:22.652
A sand crab.

157
12:23.583 --> 12:25.333
It's quite lively.

158
12:25.333 --> 12:26.583
Yeah.

159
12:26.583 --> 12:27.833
In this environment,

160
12:27.833 --> 12:30.316
I'll keep it alive as long as I can.

161
12:30.316 --> 12:33.875
By the way, weren't you interested in my research before?

162
12:33.875 --> 12:35.666
I asked Dao to get some equipment,

163
12:35.666 --> 12:37.166
and set up a simple lab.

164
12:37.166 --> 12:38.920
Do you want to take a look?

165
12:39.583 --> 12:40.642
Now?

166
12:40.642 --> 12:42.226
Yeah, if it's convenient for you.

167
12:42.226 --> 12:44.185
It's not far, just next door.

168
12:46.666 --> 12:48.045
Okay.

169
12:58.375 --> 12:59.953
Come in.

170
13:14.166 --> 13:17.666
Is this all your lab equipment?

171
13:17.666 --> 13:18.791
Scavenged from all over.

172
13:18.791 --> 13:22.041
Dao and his men salvaged most of it from various medical sites.

173
13:22.041 --> 13:23.208
It's a mismatched collection.

174
13:23.208 --> 13:25.143
It's good enough that it works.

175
13:26.500 --> 13:29.026
What's in here?

176
13:38.250 --> 13:39.292
Don't be afraid.

177
13:39.292 --> 13:42.458
This is a subject I asked Dao to help me capture.

178
13:42.458 --> 13:44.875
He helps with this too?

179
13:44.875 --> 13:46.583
Researching a vaccine is a good cause.

180
13:46.583 --> 13:48.592
Of course he'd help out.

181
14:27.625 --> 14:29.065
Brother...

182
14:39.583 --> 14:41.833
This is my brother, He Yao.

183
14:41.833 --> 14:44.457
This... This is your brother?

184
14:44.457 --> 14:45.460
- Yes. - Are you sure?

185
14:45.460 --> 14:48.040
Yes, it's him.

186
14:52.541 --> 14:54.476
What will you do to him?

187
14:55.916 --> 14:57.625
If we were at Casia,

188
14:57.625 --> 14:59.916
his blood and cerebrospinal fluid would be drawn.

189
14:59.916 --> 15:01.417
Some tissues or organs would be removed

190
15:01.417 --> 15:02.791
for in vitro cultivation.

191
15:02.791 --> 15:04.583
- Or... - Enough!

192
15:04.583 --> 15:06.976
I won't let you do that to him.

193
15:08.625 --> 15:09.916
Don't be nervous.

194
15:09.916 --> 15:11.083
What I just described

195
15:11.083 --> 15:12.791
is Casia's standard experimental procedure.

196
15:12.791 --> 15:15.766
But I won't do that.

197
15:16.666 --> 15:18.292
What do you mean?

198
15:19.166 --> 15:20.500
What I really want to research

199
15:20.500 --> 15:21.666
has never been a vaccine.

200
15:21.666 --> 15:23.500
It's antiretroviral drugs.

201
15:23.500 --> 15:26.330
A cure to turn zombies back into humans.

202
15:26.330 --> 15:29.064
What? Say that again.

203
15:31.458 --> 15:32.624
My research direction

204
15:32.624 --> 15:35.418
runs counter to the goals of Casia's higher-ups.

205
15:35.418 --> 15:37.542
They believe researching a zombie cure

206
15:37.542 --> 15:40.333
would cause confusion regarding the identity of zombies,

207
15:40.333 --> 15:43.041
and lead to an uncontrollable moral collapse.

208
15:43.791 --> 15:46.958
So, I was forbidden from doing such research

209
15:46.958 --> 15:49.166
and was even put under surveillance.

210
15:49.166 --> 15:51.174
So, I ran away.

211
15:56.166 --> 16:00.000
Simply put, Casia doesn't see zombies as humans.

212
16:00.000 --> 16:01.695
But I do.

213
16:03.708 --> 16:05.490
Come with me.

214
16:43.875 --> 16:45.472
Is it true?

215
16:46.166 --> 16:47.945
You can make a cure?

216
16:48.750 --> 16:50.708
No, I can't.

217
16:50.708 --> 16:52.470
At least not yet.

218
16:53.250 --> 16:54.333
Why not?

219
16:54.333 --> 16:56.083
- Isn't all this... - This vial of test fluid

220
16:56.083 --> 16:58.375
was synthesized using everything I could get my hands on back then.

221
16:58.375 --> 16:59.583
But the results are extremely unstable

222
16:59.583 --> 17:00.917
and cannot be replicated.

223
17:00.917 --> 17:03.708
The key problem is, I'm missing a specific antibody

224
17:03.708 --> 17:06.458
that can neutralize and reverse the virus.

225
17:06.458 --> 17:08.750
Theoretically, this antibody is most likely

226
17:08.750 --> 17:09.750
to be found in a very small number of cases

227
17:09.750 --> 17:11.125
who have been infected with the virus

228
17:11.125 --> 17:14.035
but have not turned into zombies.

229
17:17.250 --> 17:18.458
I was bitten by a zombie.

230
17:18.458 --> 17:19.750
But I didn't mutate.

231
17:19.750 --> 17:22.822
Do I have this antibody in my body?

232
17:25.125 --> 17:27.708
You... You're an immune.

233
17:27.708 --> 17:30.125
Yes. I'm an immune.

234
17:30.125 --> 17:32.375
Can you make a cure now?

235
17:32.375 --> 17:33.625
Yes.

236
17:33.625 --> 17:34.708
I can.

237
17:34.708 --> 17:36.565
I'm sure I can.

238
17:43.458 --> 17:45.500
I can help you with the experiment.

239
17:45.500 --> 17:46.958
But you have to swear...

240
17:46.958 --> 17:48.968
that you'll turn my brother back into a human.

241
17:49.834 --> 17:52.392
Okay. I swear.

242
17:53.791 --> 17:55.916
But you must understand...

243
17:55.916 --> 17:57.291
the experimental process

244
17:57.291 --> 17:59.208
comes with unpredictable risks.

245
17:59.208 --> 18:01.833
It might cause you harm.

246
18:01.833 --> 18:05.000
Some of it might even be irreversible.

247
18:05.000 --> 18:06.602
Are you sure?

248
18:09.458 --> 18:10.937
I'm sure.

249
18:12.083 --> 18:13.083
Good.

250
18:13.083 --> 18:16.505
You must not let anyone know about this.

251
18:17.543 --> 18:19.375
This fuel already belongs to someone.

252
18:19.375 --> 18:21.166
Besides, we're not in a hurry to leave.

253
18:21.166 --> 18:23.166
Are you not in a hurry to leave,

254
18:23.166 --> 18:25.554
or do you just not want to come with me?

255
18:30.291 --> 18:32.750
Is it possible that one day,

256
18:32.750 --> 18:34.541
zombies could turn back into humans?

257
18:34.541 --> 18:36.625
A zombie is a zombie.

258
18:36.625 --> 18:38.319
They can't turn back.

259
18:46.875 --> 18:48.208
Okay.
